or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Simple Present Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span> tense: <ul><li>to talk about things that are always true</li> <li>to give general information</li> <li>to talk about habits and routines</li> <li>with stative verbs like <span class=\"italic\">to be, to seem, to feel</span></li></ul>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You're right on schedule! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I always bake plenty of sweet treats.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I saut\u00e9 them a bit so they're crunchy!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Present  and the Present Continuous tenses to talk about the present in different ways. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quantities and Measures", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you cook, you use measures. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item. Quantifiers do not indicate a specific quantity but rather a general amount.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a/an/one</br> some</br> plenty of</br> lots of</br> a few / a little</br> a bunch</br> a mouthful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a single item</br> a general amount</br> more than is needed</br> a large amount</br> a small number or amount</br> a group</br> enough to fit in the mouth</br> comfortably\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You laid bunches of holly on the table!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Every mouthful is perfect.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are lots of almonds with the vegetables too! ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to have seconds", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a second plate of food", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're having seconds already! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about Christmas dinner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "crunchy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "makes sounds when eating", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These sauteed almonds are nice and crunchy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stuffing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a filling baked inside a turkey or vegetable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The stuffing has chestnuts in it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to roast", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cook in the oven", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to roast the turkey for several hours! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "mincemeat", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bsweet, \u200bspicy \u200bmixture \u200bof apple, \u200bdried \u200bfruit, and \u200bnuts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do I smell mincemeat pie?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "holly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small evergreen tree with red berries", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You put bunches of holly on the table! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "mouthful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "what fits comfortably in your mouth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Every mouthful of this dinner is perfect!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look up the instructions for something you like to eat at Christmas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the ingredients.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down instructions using  the Imperative.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell a partner how to put together the food. Use the Imperative.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look up a Christmas food or drink.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write down the ingredients and instructions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tell my partner how to make it. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le18ob02re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le18ob02re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Peter! Merry Christmas!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Do I smell mincemeat pie?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes, you do. I always bake plenty of sweet treats.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: No diets this week!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Here are a few gifts for under the tree."}, {"image": "engenn6le18ob02re2img06.jpg", "time": "13000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sit down. The food is almost ready.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: 1 p.m., right on schedule! How do you do that?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Training!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You laid bunches of holly on the table!"}, {"image": "engenn6le18ob02re2img06.jpg", "time": "21000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Dig in!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Mmm. What do you add to your cranberry sauce?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: A cup of orange juice and a little ginger.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Amazing!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Does this turkey have chestnuts and raisins in it?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes. It's roasted with a different type of stuffing."}, {"image": "engenn6le18ob02re2img02.jpg", "time": "36000", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: There are lots of almonds with the vegetables too! </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I saut\u00e9 them a bit so they're crunchy.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I've never had nuts with vegetables before! You mixed the yams and potatoes and grilled them right?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Uhm hum.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Every mouthful is perfect. Vanessa. Some day you are going to be a  famous chef!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Thank you.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Peter! You're having seconds already?</br>\n<span class=